IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- LAYER 1, part ssc2, module 1 of 6: Part II, Preliminary, ss 20 and 21.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-1992-4.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from
-- legislation.gov.uk (point in time 2026-07-08). It is not the official text and nothing here is
-- "verified against the official text". The rendering OMITS the table of s 21(2).
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE is the Act answering in its own words;
-- NOTHING is "not covered" and a caller must never turn it into FALSE (NOTES.md has the rule).
-- Every branch that answers "no" carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`; every "not covered" branch
-- carries `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.

§ `Part II -- Contributory Benefits: Preliminary (ss 20 and 21)`

§§ `s 20 Descriptions of contributory benefits`

-- src:714 | (1) Contributory benefits under this Part of this Act are of the following descriptions, namely—
-- src:715 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:716 | (b) incapacity benefit, comprising—
-- src:717 | (i) short-term incapacity benefit, and
-- src:718 | (ii) long-term incapacity benefit;
-- src:719 | (d) maternity allowance ... ;
-- src:720 | (e) widow’s benefit, comprising—
-- src:721 | (i) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:722 | (ii) widowed mother’s allowance ... ;
-- src:723 | (iii) widow’s pension;
-- src:724 | (ea) widowed parent's allowance;
-- src:725 | (f) retirement pensions of the following categories—
-- src:726 | (i) Category A, payable to a person by virtue of his own contributions (with increase for adult ... dependants); and
-- src:727 | (ii) Category B, payable to a person by virtue of the contributions of a spouse ... or civil partner
-- src:728 | (fa) shared additional pensions;
-- src:729 | (g) for existing beneficiaries only, child’s special allowance.
@ref s 20(1) (src:714-729)
-- The list says "are of the following descriptions, namely"; it does not say "only", so a benefit
-- that is not on it is NOT COVERED here, not a "no". The one "only" in the list is limb (g).
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
      `the person is an existing beneficiary of child's special allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(1) the benefit is a contributory benefit under this Part` MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN `short-term incapacity benefit` THEN JUST TRUE         -- (b)(i)
    WHEN `long-term incapacity benefit` THEN JUST TRUE          -- (b)(ii)
    WHEN `maternity allowance` THEN JUST TRUE                   -- (d)
    WHEN `widowed mother's allowance` THEN JUST TRUE            -- (e)(ii)
    WHEN `widow's pension` THEN JUST TRUE                       -- (e)(iii)
    WHEN `widowed parent's allowance` THEN JUST TRUE            -- (ea)
    WHEN `Category A retirement pension` THEN JUST TRUE         -- (f)(i)
    WHEN `Category B retirement pension` THEN JUST TRUE         -- (f)(ii)
    WHEN `shared additional pension` THEN JUST TRUE             -- (fa)
    WHEN `child's special allowance` THEN                       -- (g)
        IF `the person is an existing beneficiary of child's special allowance`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for existing beneficiaries only, child’s special allowance"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "namely" does not close the list with "only"; a benefit named in another Part is not decided here

-- src:730 | (2) In this Act—
-- src:731 | “long-term benefit” means—
-- src:732 | long-term incapacity benefit;
-- src:733 | a widowed mother’s allowance;
-- src:734 | a widowed parent’s allowance;
-- src:736 | a widow’s pension; and
-- src:737 | a Category A or Category B retirement pension
-- src:738 | a shared additional pension;; and
@ref s 20(2) “long-term benefit” (src:730-738)
-- A definition that says "means": a benefit that is not on the list is not a long-term benefit.
-- The blank entry (src:735) is shown repealed or blank in this text.
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(2) the benefit is a long-term benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN `long-term incapacity benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `widowed mother's allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `widowed parent's allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `widow's pension` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Category A retirement pension` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Category B retirement pension` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `shared additional pension` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“long-term benefit” means—"

-- src:739 | “short-term benefit” means—
-- src:741 | short-term incapacity benefit; and
-- src:742 | maternity allowance.
@ref s 20(2) “short-term benefit” (src:739-742)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(2) the benefit is a short-term benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN `short-term incapacity benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `maternity allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“short-term benefit” means—"

-- src:743 | (3) The provisions of this Part of this Act are subject to the provisions of Chapter II of Part III of the Pensions Act (reduction in benefits for members of schemes that were contracted-out).
@ref s 20(3) (src:743)
-- Chapter II of Part III of the Pensions Act is not among the sources: whether a person is a
-- member of a scheme that was contracted-out is a borrowed fact, asked as an input.
-- "Subject to" says the Pensions Act reduction takes precedence where it applies; it does not say
-- what happens to a person it does not reach.
GIVEN `the person is a member of a scheme that was contracted-out (Chapter II of Part III of the Pensions Act)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(3) the provisions of this Part are subject to the Pensions Act reduction` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of a scheme that was contracted-out (Chapter II of Part III of the Pensions Act)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text makes the Part subject to those provisions, and says nothing of a person they do not reach

§§ `s 21 Contribution conditions`

-- src:745 | (1) Entitlement to any of the benefits specified in section 20(1) above, other than short-term incapacity benefit under subsection (1)(b) of section 30A below, long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (5) of that section , maternity allowance under section 35 or 35B below or short-term or long-term incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41 below or a shared additional pension under section 55A or 55AA below, depends on contribution conditions being satisfied (either by the claimant or by some other person, according to the particular benefit).
@ref s 21(1) (src:745)
-- The routes of entitlement that s 21(1) carves out. Every constructor begins with the label.
DECLARE `s 21(1) Route of entitlement` IS ONE OF
    `s 21(1) any route not carved out`
    `s 21(1) short-term incapacity benefit under section 30A(1)(b)`
    `s 21(1) long-term incapacity benefit under section 30A(5)`
    `s 21(1) maternity allowance under section 35`
    `s 21(1) maternity allowance under section 35B`
    `s 21(1) incapacity benefit under section 40`
    `s 21(1) incapacity benefit under section 41`
    `s 21(1) shared additional pension under section 55A`
    `s 21(1) shared additional pension under section 55AA`

@ref s 21(1) (src:745)
-- "other than" carves the listed routes out of the sentence, in the text's own words; the
-- function says whether the s 21(1) requirement applies, and not whether the carved-out
-- routes have conditions of their own (they do, in the sections named).
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
      `the person is an existing beneficiary of child's special allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      route IS A `s 21(1) Route of entitlement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(1) the requirement of contribution conditions applies to the entitlement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 20(1) the benefit is a contributory benefit under this Part` benefit `the person is an existing beneficiary of child's special allowance`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER route
        WHEN `s 21(1) any route not carved out` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 21(1) short-term incapacity benefit under section 30A(1)(b)` THEN
            IF benefit EQUALS `short-term incapacity benefit` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than short-term incapacity benefit under subsection (1)(b) of section 30A below"
            ELSE NOTHING                                                         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the route does not belong to this benefit
        WHEN `s 21(1) long-term incapacity benefit under section 30A(5)` THEN
            IF benefit EQUALS `long-term incapacity benefit` THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "long-term incapacity benefit under subsection (5) of that section"
            ELSE NOTHING                                                         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the route does not belong to this benefit
        WHEN `s 21(1) maternity allowance under section 35` THEN
            IF benefit EQUALS `maternity allowance` THEN JUST FALSE              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "maternity allowance under section 35 or 35B below"
            ELSE NOTHING                                                         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the route does not belong to this benefit
        WHEN `s 21(1) maternity allowance under section 35B` THEN
            IF benefit EQUALS `maternity allowance` THEN JUST FALSE              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "maternity allowance under section 35 or 35B below"
            ELSE NOTHING                                                         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the route does not belong to this benefit
        WHEN `s 21(1) incapacity benefit under section 40` THEN
            IF benefit EQUALS `short-term incapacity benefit` OR benefit EQUALS `long-term incapacity benefit` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "short-term or long-term incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41 below"
            ELSE NOTHING                                                         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the route does not belong to this benefit
        WHEN `s 21(1) incapacity benefit under section 41` THEN
            IF benefit EQUALS `short-term incapacity benefit` OR benefit EQUALS `long-term incapacity benefit` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "short-term or long-term incapacity benefit under section 40 or 41 below"
            ELSE NOTHING                                                         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the route does not belong to this benefit
        WHEN `s 21(1) shared additional pension under section 55A` THEN
            IF benefit EQUALS `shared additional pension` THEN JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a shared additional pension under section 55A or 55AA below"
            ELSE NOTHING                                                         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the route does not belong to this benefit
        WHEN `s 21(1) shared additional pension under section 55AA` THEN
            IF benefit EQUALS `shared additional pension` THEN JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a shared additional pension under section 55A or 55AA below"
            ELSE NOTHING                                                         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the route does not belong to this benefit
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the benefit is not one that s 20(1) names as contributory in a case that is decided here
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): s 20(1) does not decide the benefit

-- src:746 | (2) The class or classes of contribution which, for the purposes of subsection (1) above, are relevant in relation to each of those benefits are as follows—
@ref s 21(2) (src:746)
-- The table that follows this sentence is OMITTED from the text (PLAN.md 1.5). The classes the table
-- gives for the benefit are therefore an input; with no table the answer is NOTHING.
GIVEN `the classes of contribution the table of section 21(2) specifies for the benefit` IS A MAYBE (LIST OF `Class of contribution`)
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Class of contribution`)
`s 21(2) the classes of contribution relevant to the benefit` MEANS
    `the classes of contribution the table of section 21(2) specifies for the benefit`   -- NOTHING when the table is absent: NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the table is omitted from this text

-- src:747 | (3) The relevant contribution conditions in relation to the benefits specified in subsection (2) above are those specified in Part I of Schedule 3 to this Act.
@ref s 21(3) (src:747)
-- Seam S1: Schedule 3 Part I (ssc8) answers; the contribution conditions are an input.
GIVEN `sch 3 pt I the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(3) the relevant contribution conditions are those in Schedule 3 Part I` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 3 pt I the contribution conditions for the benefit are satisfied`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 3 answers, asked as an input
    WHEN JUST satisfied THEN JUST satisfied

-- src:749 | (5) In subsection (4) above and Schedule 3 to this Act—
-- src:750 | (a) “the contributor concerned”, for the purposes of any contribution condition, means the person by whom the condition is to be satisfied;
@ref s 21(5)(a) (src:749-750)
-- A definition that says "means": the contributor concerned is the person by whom the condition is
-- to be satisfied. s 21(1) says it may be the claimant or some other person.
GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Person
      `the other person on whose contributions the benefit depends` IS A MAYBE Person
      `the condition is to be satisfied by the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Person
`s 21(5)(a) the contributor concerned` MEANS
    IF `the condition is to be satisfied by the other person`
    THEN `the other person on whose contributions the benefit depends`     -- NOTHING when no other person is named: NOTHING-kind (silent)
    ELSE JUST `the claimant`

-- src:751 | (b) “a relevant class”, in relation to any benefit, means a class of contributions specified in relation to that benefit in subsection (2) above;
@ref s 21(5)(b) (src:751)
-- A definition that says "means": a class not specified in subsection (2) for the benefit is not
-- a relevant class. With the table omitted, the list is an input and may be absent.
GIVEN `the classes of contribution the table of section 21(2) specifies for the benefit` IS A MAYBE (LIST OF `Class of contribution`)
      class IS A `Class of contribution`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(5)(b) the class is a relevant class in relation to the benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 21(2) the classes of contribution relevant to the benefit` `the classes of contribution the table of section 21(2) specifies for the benefit`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the table of s 21(2) is omitted from this text
    WHEN JUST classes THEN
        IF elem class classes
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE           -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“a relevant class”, in relation to any benefit, means a class of contributions specified in relation to that benefit in subsection (2) above"

-- src:752 | (c) “the earnings factor”—
-- src:753 | (i) where the year in question is 1987-88 or any subsequent tax year, means, in relation to a person, the aggregate of his earnings factors derived from so much of his earnings as did not exceed the upper earnings limit and upon which primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid and from his Class 2 and Class 3 contributions; and
-- src:754 | (ii) where the year in question is any earlier tax year, means, in relation to a person’s contributions of any class or classes, the aggregate of his earnings factors derived from all those contributions;
@ref s 21(5)(c) (src:752-754)
-- Which paragraph of (c) governs depends on the year in question, in the text's own words.
DECLARE `s 21(5)(c) Paragraph that governs the year` IS ONE OF
    `s 21(5)(c)(i) the year is 1987-88 or a later tax year`
    `s 21(5)(c)(ii) the year is an earlier tax year`

GIVEN year IS A `Tax year`
GIVETH A `s 21(5)(c) Paragraph that governs the year`
`s 21(5)(c) the paragraph that governs the year` MEANS
    IF year's `calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST 1987
    THEN `s 21(5)(c)(i) the year is 1987-88 or a later tax year`
    ELSE `s 21(5)(c)(ii) the year is an earlier tax year`

@ref s 21(5)(c)(i) (src:753)
-- "means ... the aggregate of his earnings factors derived from [earnings up to the upper earnings
-- limit with primary Class 1 contributions paid] and from his Class 2 and Class 3 contributions".
-- Each earnings factor is a number of pounds the tables of s 23(1)(b) give; here each is an input.
GIVEN `the earnings factor derived from earnings not exceeding the upper earnings limit on which primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the earnings factor derived from Class 2 contributions` IS A NUMBER
      `the earnings factor derived from Class 3 contributions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21(5)(c)(i) the earnings factor for a year from 1987-88` MEANS
    `the earnings factor derived from earnings not exceeding the upper earnings limit on which primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid`
        PLUS `the earnings factor derived from Class 2 contributions`
        PLUS `the earnings factor derived from Class 3 contributions`

@ref s 21(5)(c)(ii) (src:754)
-- "the aggregate of his earnings factors derived from all those contributions" (earlier years).
GIVEN `the earnings factors derived from each of the contributions` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21(5)(c)(ii) the earnings factor for an earlier year` MEANS
    sum `the earnings factors derived from each of the contributions`

-- src:755 | (d) except in the expression “benefit year”, “year” means a tax year.
@ref s 21(5)(d) (src:755)
DECLARE `s 21(5)(d) Meaning of year` IS ONE OF
    `s 21(5)(d) a tax year`
    `s 21(5)(d) the period defined in subsection (6)`

GIVEN `the expression is "benefit year"` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 21(5)(d) Meaning of year`
`s 21(5)(d) what year means` MEANS
    IF `the expression is "benefit year"`
    THEN `s 21(5)(d) the period defined in subsection (6)`   -- the exception in the text: "except in the expression “benefit year”"
    ELSE `s 21(5)(d) a tax year`

-- src:756 | (5A) Where primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid on any part of a person’s earnings, the following provisions, namely—
-- src:757 | (a) subsection (5)(c) above;
-- src:758 | (b) sections 22(1)(a) , (2A) and (3)(a), 23(3)(a), 24(2)(a), 44(6)(za) and (a) ... below; and
-- src:759 | (c) paragraphs 2(4)(a) and (5)(a), 4(2)(a), 5(2)(b) and (4)(a) , 5A(3)(a) and 7(4)(a) of Schedule 3 to this Act,
-- src:760 | shall have effect as if such contributions had been paid or treated as paid on so much of the earnings as did not exceed the upper earnings limit.
@ref s 21(5A) (src:756-760)
-- Where primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid on part of the earnings,
-- the listed provisions work as if they had been paid on so much of the earnings as did not exceed
-- the upper earnings limit.
GIVEN earnings IS A NUMBER
      `the upper earnings limit` IS A NUMBER
      `primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid on part of the earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 21(5A) the earnings on which contributions are treated as paid` MEANS
    IF `primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid on part of the earnings`
    THEN JUST (IF earnings AT MOST `the upper earnings limit` THEN earnings ELSE `the upper earnings limit`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text applies "Where primary Class 1 contributions have been paid or treated as paid on any part of a person’s earnings"

@ref s 21(5A) (src:756-760)
-- The provisions that s 21(5A)(a) to (c) mention, spelt as the text cites them (Schedule 3
-- paragraphs are written "sch 3 para ..." because the converter dropped the paragraph numbers).
-- Seam S8: ssc1 s 6A asks whether a provision is one of these.
`s 21(5A) the provisions mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (c)` MEANS
    LIST "21(5)(c)"
       , "22(1)(a)"
       , "22(2A)"
       , "22(3)(a)"
       , "23(3)(a)"
       , "24(2)(a)"
       , "44(6)(za)"
       , "44(6)(a)"
       , "sch 3 para 2(4)(a)"
       , "sch 3 para 2(5)(a)"
       , "sch 3 para 4(2)(a)"
       , "sch 3 para 5(2)(b)"
       , "sch 3 para 5(4)(a)"
       , "sch 3 para 5A(3)(a)"
       , "sch 3 para 7(4)(a)"

@ref s 21(5A) (src:756-760)
GIVEN provision IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(5A) the provision is one mentioned in section 21(5A)(a) to (c)` MEANS
    IF elem provision `s 21(5A) the provisions mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the following provisions, namely" does not close the list with "only"

§§ `s 21(6) Benefit year`

-- src:761 | (6) In this Part of this Act “benefit year” means a period—
-- src:762 | (a) beginning with the first Sunday in January in any calendar year, and
-- src:763 | (b) ending with the Saturday immediately preceding the first Sunday in January in the following calendar year;
-- src:764 | but for any prescribed purposes of this Part of this Act “benefit year” may by regulations be made to mean such other period (whether or not a period of 12 months) as may be specified in the regulations.
@ref s 21(6) (src:761-764)
-- The weekday of a date, 0 for Sunday ... 6 for Saturday, counted from 1 January 2023, which was
-- a Sunday. The count is taken from a calendar fact, not from the Act.
GIVEN date IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21(6)(a) the weekday of the date, 0 for Sunday` MEANS
    (((Day date) MINUS (Day (Date 1 1 2023))) MODULO 7 PLUS 7) MODULO 7

-- (a) "beginning with the first Sunday in January in any calendar year"
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 21(6)(a) the first Sunday in January of the year` MEANS
    (Date 1 1 year) PLUS ((7 MINUS `s 21(6)(a) the weekday of the date, 0 for Sunday` (Date 1 1 year)) MODULO 7)

-- (b) "ending with the Saturday immediately preceding the first Sunday in January in the following
-- calendar year"
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 21(6)(b) the last day of the benefit year that begins in the year` MEANS
    (`s 21(6)(a) the first Sunday in January of the year` (year PLUS 1)) MINUS 1

-- The proviso: "but for any prescribed purposes of this Part of this Act “benefit year” may by
-- regulations be made to mean such other period (whether or not a period of 12 months)".
-- The other period is an input; with none, the benefit year is the one in (a) and (b).
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the other period the regulations specify for the prescribed purpose` IS A MAYBE Period
GIVETH A Period
`s 21(6) the benefit year that begins in the calendar year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the other period the regulations specify for the prescribed purpose`
    WHEN JUST other THEN other
    WHEN NOTHING THEN Period WITH
        `the first day` IS `s 21(6)(a) the first Sunday in January of the year` year
        `the last day` IS `s 21(6)(b) the last day of the benefit year that begins in the year` year
